      "edition": "122nd edition, effective January 1, 2026",
      "note": "Basic personal amounts, the federal phase-out, the Manitoba and Yukon formulas, the 16.5% Quebec abatement on basic federal tax, Ontario surtax, Ontario health premium, and the Ontario basic tax reduction. The January table still shows Newfoundland and Labrador at $11,188."
    },
    "t4127_july": {
      "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/forms-publications/payroll/t4127-payroll-deductions-formulas/t4127-jul/t4127-jul-payroll-deductions-formulas.html",
      "edition": "123rd edition, effective July 1, 2026",
      "note": "Newfoundland and Labrador's basic personal amount rose from $11,188 to $13,094 effective January 1, 2026. Payroll uses $15,000 in the second half of 2026 as a catch-up. This estimate uses $13,094. The same edition says British Columbia's annual lowest rate is 5.60% and that the 6.14% rate is the payroll catch-up."
    },
